(3211423, 450760, 30049, '<td valign="top">Something doesn''t quite fit telling this story...maybe it''s the pencil being back at the beginning of the sentence on the paper?  The proper writing position of the hand?  The lighting comes across as dark, emotive, broody (is that a word?).  Perhaps if the pencil was broken and splintered with the hand nearby clenched in a fist?  I''m wondering also about the area in the upper left.  Haven''t decided if it''s right, wrong, or indifferent.  All I know is I''ve noticed it and it pulls the eye out of the center of the frame.<br/> <br/>All of the above is JMO of course.  :D  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'Something doesn''t quite fit telling this story...maybe it''s the pencil being back at the beginning of the sentence on the paper?  The proper writing position of the hand?  The lighting comes across as dark, emotive, broody (is that a word?).  Perhaps if the pencil was broken and splintered with the hand nearby clenched in a fist?  I''m wondering also about the area in the upper left.  Haven''t decided if it''s right, wrong, or indifferent.  All I know is I''ve noticed it and it pulls the eye out of the center of the frame. All of the above is JMO of course.  :D  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2007-01-11 09:31:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(3211427, 450839, 49109, '<td valign="top">good shot, had been even better with less reflections on the picture frame</td>', 'good shot, had been even better with less reflections on the picture frame', '2007-01-11 09:32:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(3211439, 450558, 30049, '<td valign="top">I like the POV you used in capturing this photo and the strong diagonal line.  The sky works in your favor also.  Being advanced editing I''d have cloned out that little piece of tree branches showing in the bottom left.  :D  The sharpest area of this image is around the feet and lower legs.  I think I''d have tried to put the focus more on the head and chest area - not that the upper areas are badly OOF or anything, just a tad soft. The score on this will probably hit the center with polarizing votes based on subject matter.  Hope you knew that going in.  Overall, well done.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'I like the POV you used in capturing this photo and the strong diagonal line.  The sky works in your favor also.  Being advanced editing I''d have cloned out that little piece of tree branches showing in the bottom left.  :D  The sharpest area of this image is around the feet and lower legs.  I think I''d have tried to put the focus more on the head and chest area - not that the upper areas are badly OOF or anything, just a tad soft. The score on this will probably hit the center with polarizing votes based on subject matter.  Hope you knew that going in.  Overall, well done.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2007-01-11 09:35:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(3211440, 448253, 49109, '<td valign="top">very nicely displayed, quite artsy. were gone for a more decent frame, though</td>', 'very nicely displayed, quite artsy. were gone for a more decent frame, though', '2007-01-11 09:35:52.000000', NULL, 1),
